      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Although various case-control studies have been conducted to investigate the relationship between ADRB2 gene polymorphisms and asthma risk in different population groups, the results have been conflicting and inconclusive."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "We performed a case-control study to investigate the association of 4 SNPs in the ADRB2 gene with risk of asthma in children, and then conducted a meta-analysis by combining the previous studies."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "A total of 340 patients and 340 age-matched healthy controls were recruited. All of the subjects were genotyped using the PCR-based invader assay. The case-control study was performed to define the contribution of rs1042713, rs1042714, rs1800888, and rs1042711 to the predisposition of asthma. Additionally, we further conducted a meta-analysis of the study findings together with those of previously reported studies."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "No significant association was found between the polymorphisms rs1042713, rs1042714, rs1800888, and rs1042711 and asthma in the current case-control study. The meta-analysis confirmed that there was no positive association of these SNPs with asthma in children in Asia, South America, Europe and the overall population."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "None of the four polymorphisms in ADRB2 gene were associated with a risk of asthma in a current children population."
        }
      ]},
